& [DictatedProductTarget]
  + Cantor should run from SOP do its own bounded work perform separately authorized updates and generate its own succeeding SOP proposal from the exact causal frontier
  + the self-authored SOP remains a proposal until independent semantic review satisfaction signature source preservation and activation
  + Cantor is also intended to become the slim launch pad for a larger nested Cantor and LLM system but that process model and shared-attention authority remains separate

& [CurrentPublishedSubstrate]
  + SWA-01 admitted SOP to proposed-not-launched session identity is published
  + SWA-02 objective-bound work-plan admission is published
  + SWA-03 deterministic lifecycle and checkpoints are published
  + SWA-04A pure update handoff awaiting physical revalidation is published while SWA-04B B1 through B5 physical stages remain inactive
  + SWA-06A pure attributable succeeding-SOP proposal and independent machine verification are published at implementation checkpoint 5809f2b3da2d1f3f8187b96032c973ede2cb1881 with bookend be06cdd41d28df47a730bcf616396d60a38c5252
  + the pinned local provider remains unavailable and this slice must neither contact nor substitute one

& [RequestedSlice]
  + form the smallest provider-free SWA-07 integration joining the existing unmodified SWA-01 through SWA-04A and SWA-06A forms
  + accept one strict supplied-data request containing the SWA-04A handoff request and later SWA-06A succeeding-SOP request
  + require both to carry the exact same validated lifecycle request
  + require the handoff checkpoint transition sequence to be an exact prefix of the later checkpoint
  + require the handoff selected step to be exactly class propose_update and ready at the handoff checkpoint
  + require that same attempt to become complete in the later checkpoint before the propose_succeeding_sop step becomes ready
  + require one bounded bridge evidence reference to occur in the handoff evidence and in a post-prefix transition for that exact update attempt
  + recompile the exact update handoff proposal and succeeding-SOP proposal then independently verify the succeeding-SOP machine receipt
  + emit one deterministic self-contained correspondence receipt binding boot plan lifecycle pre-update handoff post-update and succeeding-SOP identities with domain-separated digests
  + expose compile and verify through a strict bounded stdin/stdout CLI with no output-path option

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + status is provider_free_chain_correspondence_verified and authority is supplied_data_correspondence_only
  + physical_contact is false and every embedded workspace admission or external receipt remains a supplied internally checked claim rather than a fresh observation
  + no SOP bytes workspace Git tree provider model process environment clock network filesystem mutation test execution update acceptance rollback cleanup commit push semantic review satisfaction signature persistence activation remote FPGA Minecraft or external effect is performed or granted
  + no existing SWA request proposal lifecycle handoff or succeeding-SOP semantics may be modified to make the join pass

& [VerificationTarget]
  + deterministic positive replay and strict machine-form round trips
  + refusals for profile identity lifecycle substitution checkpoint-prefix tamper wrong step classes nonready or incomplete update attempt bridge-evidence absence or laundering succeeding-SOP substitution authority widening digest tamper unknown fields oversized input extra CLI arguments and output-path attempts
  + static absence of process filesystem network provider unsafe environment and output-path product surfaces
  + focused debug overflow-checked release warnings-denied Clippy format exact workspace gates content-addressed provider-free evidence recursive evidence local acceptance attribution commit push and post-push replay

& [StopRules]
  + stop rather than import physical SWA-04B B1-through-B5 behavior or SWA-05 publication authority
  + stop rather than perform semantic review issue a signature persist or activate the generated SOP
  + stop rather than contact download substitute or remotely access a model or provider
  + stop rather than edit stage delete or claim AGENTS Minecraft Zeta Alpha neural other-conversation output temporary or foreign work

& [UnresolvedFrontier]
  + SWA-07 P0 proves composition of published pure supplied-data seams but not actual work update publication or SOP activation
  + SWA-06B independent review signature preservation and activation remains separate
  + SWA-04B B1-through-B5 and SWA-05 remain separately commissioned physical boundaries
  + SWA-08 remains conditional on exact pinned local provider and model availability
